A||||5||Wade87GT||Something to learn from my repair horror story.||||8||
Z||000000||Wade87GT||08-28-2000||08:39 PM||||My 87 GT 2.8 with A/C and 5-speed started running very rough/stalling at low RPM and under load. Ran great above 2500 RPM. I've had this car since '89/11,000 miles and most all repairs I do myself. I changed the cap/rotor, plug wires (plugs were clean) and got a code for TPS (changed the sensor). Also cleaned the K+N air filter. Still ran bad, I needed the car fixed, didn't have the time to do the rest myself, so I limped my daily driver to the shop. They called, diagnostics came up empty but the EGR tube was cracked. It didn't have the higher RPM associated with that before and I sprayed WD-40 all over looking for a vacuum leak myself, which I didn't find. $450. for a EGR tube change job that didn't fix the problem. Now they're saying low fuel pressure (20 PSI instead of 45-47 required), a bad fuel pump. Another $380. ($100. mark-up on the pump). Car runs great now. I sure hope it wasn't just bad gas or a clogged fuel filter. I have done much more difficult work before (fixing F-4 Phantom Jets) but they had me. Moral of the story? Check/do as much of the obvious as you can. Maybe I should have changed that filter myself.||||reg||8
Z||000001||My7Fieros||08-28-2000||09:18 PM||||Wade Id have to say that you got seriously boned on prices. $450 for an egr tube? I made one by welding the two end piece of a bad tube to a flex line gas hose (originally made for gas fireplaces)...cost me 5 bucks and has worked great! Its also easier because of the  screw on fittings...I can unscrew the ends and take the tube right off!<BR>Also you paid way too much for a fuel pump. Oh well, at least your car is running good again. Since you're now a member of the forum, posts your questions and problems on here before taking it up the rear from a mechanic! This place has saved me time and money that I could never put a price on!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||08-28-2000||09:35 PM||||Yep, hosed big time.  I get EGR tubes from the Pick-n-Pull all the time for $8 and it takes 15 minutes to change it.  Of course it is really easy with the ratcheting 10mm wrench that I got from ACE hardware for $8.  For $450 you could have had the $90 stainless braided tube that will never break.  As for the fuel pump, that is a little harder to replace.  I have done mine and it cost about $70, but not everyone will want to do that one.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||08-28-2000||10:30 PM||||Hey Wade, do you live anywhere near Niceville High School??  When I was over that way last year for one of my son's baseball games, I passed a yard with two Fieros in it.<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wade87GT||08-29-2000||11:10 AM||||Actually, they only charged me $105. for the EGR tube ($10. over dealer price) and the labor for the fuel pump was the same as the dealer. I had a spare EGR tube on hand, but like most shops, they don't install the customers' parts. The rest of it, my lack of time, combined with my need for the car is what led to this expensive story. Yes, mbramble, I do live a few blocks from Niceville H.S. but I don't think you saw my car. Mine's black with black 16" wheels from a '91 Beretta GTZ.||||reg||9
Z||000005||HugGRRRFiero||08-29-2000||11:40 AM||||Wade,<P>I was just visiting my Uncle and cousins in Niceville back in June!  I remember seeing a real nice 85 (I think) White GT and a Black 84 or 85 Coupe or SE too while I was there, didn't happen to be you did it?  My uncle works at Eglin AFB too...  Small world eh'<P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
